  "description": "This is a test of a single\u2011candidate ranked\u2011choice voting race using five ballots, each appearing exactly once. The ballots are identified by their ID numbers and show the voters\u2019 ordered preferences:\n\n- Ballot\u202f1 (ID\u202f1): first choice\u202f1, second choice\u202f2, third choice\u202f3.  \n- Ballot\u202f2 (ID\u202f2): first choice\u202f2, second choice\u202f1, third choice\u202f3.  \n- Ballot\u202f3 (ID\u202f3): first choice\u202f1, second choice\u202f3, third choice\u202f2.  \n- Ballot\u202f4 (ID\u202f4): first choice\u202f2, second choice\u202f3, third choice\u202f1.  \n- Ballot\u202f5 (ID\u202f5): first choice\u202f3, second choice\u202f1, third choice\u202f2.\n\nIn the event of ties, the predetermined tiebreak order is candidate\u202f2 first, then candidate\u202f3, and finally candidate\u202f1.\n\nThe tabulation proceeded as follows. In the first round the first\u2011choice totals were: candidate\u202f1 received 2 votes, candidate\u202f2 also received 2 votes, and candidate\u202f3 received 1 vote. Candidate\u202f3 was eliminated. After redistributing the ballot that had candidate\u202f3 as its top choice, the second round tallies were: candidate\u202f1 with 3 votes and candidate\u202f2 with 2 votes. No further eliminations were required, and candidate\u202f1 emerged as the winner of the election."
